Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 06:39:17 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 19/28] (b) v2, part b-3: usrguide: what the caption package
 supports

Round-3 findings R3-M2 and R3-L4 (usrguide part). usrguide ended the
list of packages and classes that replace \caption with "The caption
package supports \caption* with all of them". That is false: with
\usepackage{caption}, aastex701 and mnras print \caption* with the
number of the previous caption ("Figure 1. Starred", no warning), and
tufte-book still gives "Figure 2: *" and a list entry (the same on
TeX Live 2026 with caption v3.6o, with v3.7 and with the client on
this branch). It is true for hyperref, beamer and float (and for
uwthesis and jmlr).

The sentence now names only hyperref, beamer and float and says that
caption does not help with every class that replaces \caption. The
journal classes are no longer named in usrguide (they were marked up as
packages); "some journal and thesis classes" instead, the list stays in
ltfloat.dtx.
